            ("What to prepare", ["Prepare a supported raster image, choose the processing width or height and physical pixel size, then enable only the Rasterizer swatches you want represented in the output. A cleaner source image with fewer stray pixels, compression artifacts, and tiny color variations usually produces fewer vector objects and smaller SVG and LightBurn project files.", {"before": "If you are preparing a Material Library-backed job for the first time, LightBurn's official ", "link_text": "Material Library guide", "url": LIGHTBURN_MATERIAL_LIBRARY_DOCS, "after": " explains how its libraries, materials, entries, and cut settings are organized."}, {"before": "You can also use Rasterizer's ", "link_text": "Palette Library Generator", "link_slug": "blank-palette-library", "after": " to download a blank library populated with disabled UNCONFIGURED entries for the default Rasterizer swatches; add your tested settings, enable output, and remove UNCONFIGURED from each configured entry's Description and setting name before use."}, "Because the generated template already uses Rasterizer's expected material, entry, and swatch structure, you can focus on supplying and testing your laser settings instead of building a compatible library layout from scratch."]),
