            ("Why SVG-only mode exists", ["Reliable laser settings can represent hours of testing, consumed material, careful observation, and hard-earned experience with a particular machine. Some operators are comfortable sharing those recipes, while others reasonably treat them as private or commercially valuable information. SVG-only mode lets you use Rasterizer without uploading or otherwise providing your laser settings.", "Not every laser or controller is compatible with LightBurn. Your machine, materials, support requirements, or preferred workflow may be better served by different laser software. SVG-only mode lets those workflows use the Rasterizer as a raster-artwork-to-layered-vector converter.", {"before": "See the broader ", "link_text": "laser engraving tool", "path": "/laser-engraving-tool", "after": " overview for non-MOPA and non-color artwork workflows."}, {"before": "Operators whose laser and controller work with LightBurn can also use ", "link_text": "Hatch Palettes", "link_slug": "hatch-palettes", "after": " to map artwork colors to tested hatch directions and line densities rather than MOPA Laser color recipes."}]),
